diagonalizeViaCongruence -- diagonalizes a symmetric matrix via congruence
**************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        diagonalizeViaCongruence M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a symmetric matrix over any
        field or finite étale algebras over a field
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a diagonal matrix congruent to M

Description
===========

Given a symmetric matrix M over any field or finite étale algebra over a field,
this command gives a diagonal matrix congruent to M. Note that the order in
which the diagonal terms appear is not specified.

+----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x]/(x^2 - 1)          |
|                                  |
|o1 = R                            |
|                                  |
|o1 : QuotientRing                 |
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : M = matrix(R, {{1,2},{2,x}});|
|                                  |
|             2      2             |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R              |
+----------------------------------+
|i3 : diagonalizeViaCongruence M   |
|                                  |
|o3 = | 1 0   |                    |
|     | 0 x-4 |                    |
|                                  |
|             2      2             |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R              |
+----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note getDiagonalClass: getDiagonalClass, -- produces a diagonalized form
    for any (unstable) Grothendieck-Witt class, with simplified terms on the
    diagonal
  * *note getDiagonalEntries: getDiagonalEntries, -- extracts a list of
    diagonal entries for a GrothendieckWittClass

