getDiagonalClass -- produces a diagonalized form for any (unstable) Grothendieck-Witt class, with simplified terms on the diagonal
**********************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        getDiagonalClass beta
  * Inputs:
      * beta, a *note Grothendieck-Witt Class: GrothendieckWittClass,, over a
        field or finite étale algebra over a field
      * beta, an *note Unstable Grothendieck-Witt Class:
        UnstableGrothendieckWittClass,, over a field or finite étale algebra
        over a field
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Grothendieck-Witt Class: GrothendieckWittClass,, a form
        isomorphic to $\beta$ with a diagonal Gram matrix
      * an *note Unstable Grothendieck-Witt Class:
        UnstableGrothendieckWittClass,, a class isomorphic to $\beta$ with a
        diagonal Gram matrix

Description
===========

Given a symmetric bilinear form, this method uses the *note
diagonalizeViaCongruence: diagonalizeViaCongruence, command in order to produce
a diagonal symmetric bilinear form isomorphic to $\beta$, with reduced square
classes appearing as the diagonal entries when $\beta$ is defined over
$\mathbb{C}$, $\mathbb{R}$, $\mathbb{Q}$, or finite field of characteristic not
2. In the case of an UnstableGrothendieckWittClass the function applies *note
diagonalizeViaCongruence: diagonalizeViaCongruence, to the stable part.

+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = matrix(QQ, {{9,1,7,4},{1,10,3,2},{7,3,6,7},{4,2,7,5}});|
|                                                                |
|              4       4                                         |
|o1 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : beta = makeGWuClass M;                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : getDiagonalClass beta                                      |
|                                                                |
|o3 = (| 1 0  0   0   |, -1100)                                  |
|      | 0 89 0   0   |                                          |
|      | 0 0  445 0   |                                          |
|      | 0 0  0   -55 |                                          |
|                                                                |
|o3 : UnstableGrothendieckWittClass                              |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : getDiagonalClass makeGWClass M                             |
|                                                                |
|o4 = | 1 0  0   0   |                                           |
|     | 0 89 0   0   |                                           |
|     | 0 0  445 0   |                                           |
|     | 0 0  0   -55 |                                           |
|                                                                |
|o4 : GrothendieckWittClass                                      |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

Note that the *note GrothendieckWittClass: GrothendieckWittClass, and *note
UnstableGrothendieckWittClass: UnstableGrothendieckWittClass, type caches
diagonal versions of a form once they have been computed. We can recover this
quickly in the following way.

+----------------------------------+
|i5 : beta.cache.getDiagonalClass  |
|                                  |
|o5 = (| 1 0  0   0   |, -1100)    |
|      | 0 89 0   0   |            |
|      | 0 0  445 0   |            |
|      | 0 0  0   -55 |            |
|                                  |
|o5 : UnstableGrothendieckWittClass|
+----------------------------------+

See also
