getLocalUnstableA1Degree -- computes a local unstable $\mathbb{A}^{1}$-Brouwer degree of a pointed rational function $f/g:\mathbb{P}^{1}_{k}\to\mathbb{P}^{1}_{k}$ at a root $p\in\mathbb{P}^{1}_{k}$
*****************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        getLocalUnstableA1Degree(q, p)
        getLocalUnstableA1Degree(f, g, p)
  * Inputs:
      * q, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a pointed rational
        function $f/g$ where $f,g\in k[x]$ are coprime polynomials over a field
        $k$ of characteristic not 2 and $g$ not identically zero. Over
        $\mathbb{C}$ the two-input variant is to be used as fraction fields are
        not supported over $\mathbb{C}$. Over $\mathbb{R}$, the user is
        prompted to instead do the computation over $\mathbb{Q}$ and then base
        change to $\mathbb{R}$.
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial $f\in
        k[x]$ where $k$ is a field of characteristic not 2
      * g, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial $g\in
        k[x]$ where $k$ is a field of characteristic not 2 and $g$ is not
        identically zero, such that $f/g$ is a pointed rational function
      * p, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a point
        $p\in\mathbb{P}^{1}_{k}$ corresponding to a root of the rational
        function $f/g$ in the field $k$
      * p, a *note number: (Macaulay2Doc)Number,, a point
        $p\in\mathbb{P}^{1}_{k}$ corresponding to a root of the rational
        function $f/g$ in the field $k$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * linearTolerance => a *note real number: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,, default
        value .000001, a positive real number used to determine whether roots
        of f and g are considered equal when working over the inexact field
        $\mathbb{C}$, used to put rational functions over $\mathbb{C}$ in
        reduced form by cancelling roots that agree up to the tolerance
  * Outputs:
      * an *note Unstable Grothendieck-Witt Class:
        UnstableGrothendieckWittClass,, the class
        $\text{deg}_{p}^{\mathbb{A}^{1}}(f/g)$ in the unstable
        Grothendieck-Witt group $\text{GW}^{u}(k)$

Description
===========

Given a pointed rational function $f/g:\mathbb{P}^{1}_{k}\to\mathbb{P}^{1}_{k}$
(where $(f/g)(\infty)=\infty$) and a zero $p\in\mathbb{A}^{1}_{k}$ (as $f/g$ is
pointed), we may compute its local unstable $\mathbb{A}^{1}$-Brouwer degree
valued in the unstable Grothendieck-Witt group $\text{GW}^{u}(k)$.

For mathematical background on the local unstable $\mathbb{A}^{1}$-Brouwer
degree, see *note global unstable A1-degrees: getGlobalUnstableA1Degree,.

If the rational function is non-reduced, then the reduction is computed,
checked for pointedness, and the local degree computation run on the reduction.
See *note global unstable A1-degrees: getGlobalUnstableA1Degree, for more
details.

+------------------------------------+
|i1 : frac QQ[x];                    |
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : q = (x^2 + x - 2)/(3*x + 5);   |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : getLocalUnstableA1Degree(q, -2)|
|                                    |
|               1                    |
|o3 = (| 1/3 |, -)                   |
|               3                    |
|                                    |
|o3 : UnstableGrothendieckWittClass  |
+------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note getGlobalUnstableA1Degree: getGlobalUnstableA1Degree, -- computes the
    global unstable $\mathbb{A}^{1}$-Brouwer degree of a pointed rational
    function $f/g:\mathbb{P}^{1}_{k}\to\mathbb{P}^{1}_{k}$
  * *note getLocalA1Degree: getLocalA1Degree, -- computes a local
    $\mathbb{A}^{1}$-Brouwer degree of a list of $n$ polynomials in $n$
    variables over a field $k$ at a prime ideal in the zero locus
  * *note getGlobalA1Degree: getGlobalA1Degree, -- computes the global
    $\mathbb{A}^{1}$-Brouwer degree of a list of $n$ polynomials in $n$
    variables over a field $k$
  * *note getSumDecomposition: getSumDecomposition, -- produces a simplified
    diagonal representative of a Grothendieck-Witt class or unstable
    Grothendieck-Witt class
  * *note getSumDecompositionString: getSumDecompositionString, -- produces a
    simplified string representation of a Grothendieck-Witt class or unstable
    Grothendieck-Witt class

Ways to use getLocalUnstableA1Degree:
=====================================

  * "getLocalUnstableA1Degree(RingElement,Number)"
  * "getLocalUnstableA1Degree(RingElement,RingElement)"
  * "getLocalUnstableA1Degree(RingElement,RingElement,Number)"
  * "getLocalUnstableA1Degree(RingElement,RingElement,RingElement)"

