getNorm -- Computes the norm over $k$ for an element in a finite dimensional $k$-algebra
****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        getNorm(C,a)
        getNorm(S,I,b)
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, a finite dimensional $k$-algebra
      * a, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, an element in C
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, a polynomial ring
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal in the polynomial
        ring S
      * b, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, an element in S 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the norm over $k$ for
        an element in the algebra

Description
===========

For an element in an algebra C over a field $k$ or a polynomial ring S and an
ideal I, this function computes the norm over $k$ as the determinant of the
*note getMultiplicationMatrix: getMultiplicationMatrix, of the element.

+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = QQ[x]/(x^6+x^5+x^4+x^3+x^2+x+1);               |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = toField L;                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : getNorm(F[a,b,c], ideal(a^2,b^2,c^2),1+a*b+b*c+c*a)|
|                                                        |
|o3 = 1                                                  |
|                                                        |
|o3 : F                                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = QQ[x,y]/(x^2+y^2+1, 3*x+2);                    |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : getNorm(R, 1+y*x^2)                                |
|                                                        |
|     937                                                |
|o5 = ---                                                |
|     729                                                |
|                                                        |
|o5 : QQ                                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note getMultiplicationMatrix: getMultiplicationMatrix, -- Computes the
    matrix over a $k$-basis for multiplication by an element in a finite
    dimensional $k$-algebra
  * *note getTrace: getTrace, -- Computes the trace over $k$ for an element in
    a finite dimensional $k$ -algebra

Ways to use getNorm:
====================

  * "getNorm(Ring,Ideal,Thing)"
  * "getNorm(Ring,Thing)"

For the programmer
==================

