getRank -- calculates the rank of a symmetric bilinear form
***********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        getRank(beta)
  * Inputs:
      * beta, a *note Grothendieck-Witt Class: GrothendieckWittClass,, a
        symmetric bilinear form defined over $\mathbb{Q}$
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the rank of the symmetric bilinear
        form $\beta$

Description
===========

The rank of a symmetric bilinear form is the dimension of the vector space
spanned by the vectors that are orthogonal to all other vectors in the space.
This is equivalent to the number of non-zero entries on the diagonal of a
diagonalized form.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : beta = makeDiagonalForm(QQ, (3,5,7,11))|
|                                            |
|o1 = | 3 0 0 0  |                           |
|     | 0 5 0 0  |                           |
|     | 0 0 7 0  |                           |
|     | 0 0 0 11 |                           |
|                                            |
|o1 : GrothendieckWittClass                  |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : getRank beta                           |
|                                            |
|o2 = 4                                      |
+--------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note isIsomorphicForm: isIsomorphicForm, -- determines whether two
    (unstable) Grothendieck-Witt classes over
    $\mathbb{C},\mathbb{R},\mathbb{Q}$ or a finite field of characteristic not
    2 are isomorphic.
  * *note getSignature: getSignature, -- computes the signature of a symmetric
    bilinear form over the real numbers or rational numbers

Ways to use getRank:
====================

  * "getRank(GrothendieckWittClass)"
  * "getRank(Matrix)"

For the programmer
==================

