getTrace -- Computes the trace over $k$ for an element in a finite dimensional $k$ -algebra
*******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        getTrace(C,a)
        getTrace(S,I,b)
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, a finite dimensional $k$-algebra
      * a, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, an element in C
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, a polynomial ring
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal in the polynomial
        ring S
      * b, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, an element in S
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the trace over $k$
        for an element in the algebra

Description
===========

For an element in an algebra C over a field $k$ or a polynomial ring S and an
ideal I, this function computes the trace over $k$ as the trace of the *note
getMultiplicationMatrix: getMultiplicationMatrix, of the element.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = QQ[x]/(x^6+x^5+x^4+x^3+x^2+x+1);                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = toField L;                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : getTrace(F[a,b,c], ideal(a^2,b^2,c^2),1+a*b+b*c+c*a)|
|                                                         |
|o3 = 8                                                   |
|                                                         |
|o3 : F                                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = QQ[x,y]/(x^2+y^2+1, 3*x+2);                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : getTrace(R, 1+y*x^2)                                |
|                                                         |
|o5 = 2                                                   |
|                                                         |
|o5 : QQ                                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note getMultiplicationMatrix: getMultiplicationMatrix, -- Computes the
    matrix over a $k$-basis for multiplication by an element in a finite
    dimensional $k$-algebra
  * *note getNorm: getNorm, -- Computes the norm over $k$ for an element in a
    finite dimensional $k$-algebra
  * *note transferGW: transferGW, -- the transfer of Grothendieck-Witt from an
    étale algebras to a base field

Ways to use getTrace:
=====================

  * "getTrace(Ring,Ideal,Thing)"
  * "getTrace(Ring,Thing)"

