getWittIndex -- returns the Witt index of a symmetric bilinear form
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        getWittIndex beta
  * Inputs:
      * beta, a *note Grothendieck-Witt Class: GrothendieckWittClass,, a
        GrothendieckWittClass denoted by $\beta\in\text{GW}(k)$, where $k$ is
        $\mathbb{Q}$, $\mathbb{R}$, $\mathbb{C}$, or a finite field of
        characteristic not 2
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the rank of the totally isotropic
        part of $\beta$

Description
===========

By the Witt Decomposition Theorem, any non-degenerate form decomposes uniquely
as $\beta \cong n \mathbb{H} \oplus \beta_a$ where the form $\beta_a$ is
anisotropic. The integer $n$ is called the Witt index of $\beta$. See for
instance [L05, I.4.3].

References
==========

[L05] T.Y. Lam, "Introduction to quadratic forms over fields," American
Mathematical Society, 2005.

See also
========

  * *note getAnisotropicDimension: getAnisotropicDimension, -- returns the
    anisotropic dimension of a symmetric bilinear form

Ways to use getWittIndex:
=========================

  * "getWittIndex(GrothendieckWittClass)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note getWittIndex: getWittIndex, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

